        impact: "I park elsewhere now.")

    static let courthouseKnife = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.courthouseKnife",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Carries Hunting Knife Through Courthouse Metal Detector", "Security Finds Blade Strapped Inside Boot"],
        law: "concealedWeapon",
        spec: "Carried a concealed knife on or about {D.his} person into a courthouse, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...65,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A metal detector at a courthouse beeped on {DATE}. Security found a 6-inch hunting knife strapped inside {D}'s boot. {D} was there for a traffic matter. {DL} says {D.he} forgot the knife from a camping trip.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Knife", "A 6-inch hunting knife in a boot.", .search), E(.statement, 2, "Security Officer", "The detector alarmed at the boot.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Forgot", "{DL} says {D.he} forgot it from camping.")],
        role: "Courthouse security officer",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job at the courthouse?", "\"I'm a security officer at the main entrance. I run the metal detector and check bags for everyone who enters.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"At 8:45 a.m., {D} walked through the detector, and it alarmed at about 8:46. The alarm sounded at the boot level.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I asked {D} to step aside and used a wand, which pointed to the right boot. I asked what was in it.\""), .direct("What did you find?", "\"A six-inch hunting knife strapped inside the boot. It was in a sheath fastened to the lower leg.\""), .direct("What did {D} say?", "\"{D} said {D.he} forgot it from a camping trip and was only there for a traffic matter. {D} looked surprised.\""), .direct("What happens with weapons at the courthouse?", "\"They aren't allowed past security, and it's posted at the door. We take the weapon and call a deputy.\""), .cross("Isn't it true {D} did not try to hide the knife?", "\"{D} didn't try to run or lie about it. When I asked, {D} said what it was right away.\""), .cross("Did {D} walk through the metal detector openly?", "\"Yes. {D} walked straight through, which is what someone hiding a weapon wouldn't usually do.\""), .cross("Did {D} threaten anyone?", "\"No. {D} was polite and cooperative the entire time.\""), .cross("Was the knife loose or strapped on?", "\"It was strapped on, in a sheath. It wasn't loose in a bag.\""), .cross("Did you see any camping gear on {D}?", "\"I didn't look at the car or belongings, only the boot. I don't know what gear {D} had.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} carried a knife into court.", "A forgotten blade."),
        allocution: "\"I should have checked.\"",
        truths: ("The knife was strapped on, not loose.", "A camping receipt showed {DL} had come straight from a trip and had not unpacked."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you at the courthouse?", "\"A traffic matter. I had a ticket to take care of, and I came in the morning to do it.\""), .direct("Why did you have a knife in your boot?", "\"I'd come straight from a camping trip and hadn't unpacked. I had the knife strapped on while hiking and forgot it.\""), .direct("When did you get back from the trip?", "\"The night before, late. I went to bed and got up early for court, and I put my boots on without thinking.\""), .direct("Did you walk through the detector knowing it was there?", "\"No. If I'd remembered, I would have left it in the car. I walked through without any thought.\""), .direct("What did you do when it alarmed?", "\"I stepped aside and told the officer what it was. I wasn't hiding it.\""), .direct("Do you have a receipt from the trip?", "\"Yes, a camping receipt from the last stop on the way home. I showed it to the deputy.\""), .cross("You've worn that knife for a trip, haven't you?", "\"I have, many times. It was in the boot, and I forgot to take it off.\""), .cross("The knife was strapped on, not loose?", "\"That's right. I'd put it on that way for hiking. It stays on until I take it off.\""), .cross("You didn't check your boots before leaving for the courthouse?", "\"No. I know I should have. It was early, and I wasn't thinking.\""), .cross("You knew the courthouse had a metal detector?", "\"I did. I've been there before, and I'd have left it behind if I'd thought about it.\""), .cross("You had the knife in a boot at a courthouse?", "\"Yes. I know it sounds hard to believe, but it was an honest mistake.\"")],
        openings: ("At 8:46 a.m. the courthouse metal detector alarmed on {D}, and a security officer found a six-inch hunting knife strapped inside {D}'s boot. {D} was there for a traffic matter, and the State will show carrying a knife into a courthouse is forbidden.", "{D} came straight from a camping trip, had not unpacked, and forgot a knife strapped to a boot. The defense says a person who walks openly through a metal detector is not carrying a weapon on purpose."),
        closings: ("A six-inch hunting knife, strapped to the leg, carried into a building posted against weapons. The detector found it, and it was on {D}'s body.", "{D} walked straight through the detector, answered honestly the moment asked, and had a camping receipt from the night before. Forgetting a knife is not knowingly bringing a weapon into court."),
        timeline: [(0, "8:45 a.m.: {DL} enters the courthouse."), (0, "8:46 a.m.: the detector alarms."), (0, "8:50 a.m.: the knife is found.")],
        identified: "A courthouse security officer.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let occupiedHouseNight = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.occupiedHouseNight",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Intruder Takes Purse From Kitchen While Family Sleeps Upstairs", "Dog's Bark Wakes Homeowner, Car Seen Leaving"],
        law: "burglary1",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Broke and entered the occupied dwelling of {V} at night with intent to commit larceny therein, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 3 a.m. on {DATE}, {V} woke to a barking dog and found the kitchen door open and {V.his} purse gone. {V} saw a car leave. A neighbor's camera recorded a plate, which belongs to {D}. A credit card from the purse was used at a gas station an hour later. {DL} says {D.he} lent the car to a coworker.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Neighbor Camera", "A car leaves the street at 3:05 a.m."), E(.document, 3, "Card Charge", "The stolen card used at a gas station at 4:10 a.m.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lent Car", "{DL} says a coworker borrowed the car.")],
        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("What woke you at 3 a.m.?", "\"My dog started barking. I came downstairs and found the kitchen door open and my purse gone.\""), .direct("What did you see outside?", "\"A car leaving the street. I did not see the driver, only the taillights.\""), .direct("How did the investigation continue?", "\"A neighbor's camera recorded the plate, which belongs to {D}. My credit card from the purse was used at a gas station about an hour later.\""), .direct("What did you find when you came downstairs?", "\"The kitchen door was standing open to the porch and the screen was bent. My purse, which had been on the counter, was gone with my wallet and keys.\""), .direct("What did you see from the window?", "\"A car pulling away from the curb with its lights off. It was dark and I couldn't make out the make, only that it was a mid-size sedan.\""), .direct("How did you learn the plate belonged to {D}?", "\"A neighbor's camera recorded a plate as the car left at 3:05, and a deputy looked it up. It came back to {D}.\""), .cross("You didn't see who was driving, did you?", "\"No. I only saw a car leaving. I could not make out a face.\""), .cross("The car could have been borrowed, couldn't it?", "\"Yes, it could have. I only know whose plate it was.\""), .cross("Was your door locked that night?", "\"I believed so. The kitchen door was open when I came down, and I do not know how it was opened.\""), .cross("Did you lock the kitchen door before bed?", "\"I believe so, but I'm not certain. The door has a latch that sometimes doesn't catch.\""), .cross("Did you recognize {D} or know of any connection to your home?", "\"No. I've never met {D}. I don't know anyone by that name.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's coworker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you borrow {D}'s car that night?", "\"No. I did not borrow it. I was not anywhere near that car on that night.\""), .direct("Where were you at 3 a.m.?", "\"I was at home asleep. I have no reason to be out at that hour.\""), .direct("What do you know about the car?", "\"Only that it is {D}'s. I have ridden in it before, but I did not drive it that night.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We work the same shift at the same company. We talk during breaks but we're not close friends.\""), .direct("Where were you at about 3 a.m. that night?", "\"At home asleep. I live alone and went to bed about ten.\""), .direct("Have you ever borrowed {D}'s car?", "\"Never. I have a car of my own, and {D} has never offered me the keys.\""), .cross("Does {D} say you borrowed it?", "\"Yes. {D} told deputies I had the car, and I do not know why.\""), .cross("Do you have a key to {D}'s car?", "\"I have never had a key. I only know it by riding with {D}.\""), .cross("Can anyone confirm you were home?", "\"No. I live alone, and I don't have a doorbell camera or anything like that.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever mention a problem with the car or lending it?", "\"No. I didn't know about any of this until a deputy called me.\""), .cross("Did {D} lend you the car, or did you take it without asking?", "\"{D} lent it to me. I asked in the afternoon and picked it up that evening. I was on shift at 3 a.m., so I could not have been at that house.\""), .cross("Why did you not come forward sooner about borrowing the car?", "\"I did not know what had happened until deputies called. As soon as I understood, I told them where I had been that night.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} entered a home and took a purse.", "A borrowed car."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I know it was terrifying.\"",
        truths: ("A gas station camera showed {DL} at the pump at 4:10 a.m.", "The coworker was on shift at 3 a.m."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you enter the house?", "\"No. I did not go into that house. I was not near that street.\""), .direct("Who had the car that night?", "\"A coworker borrowed it. I let the coworker use it for the evening.\""), .direct("Tell the jury where you were at 3 a.m.", "\"I was asleep at home. I work an early shift and was in bed by eleven.\""), .direct("Describe the coworker and the car in your own words.", "\"A coworker asked to borrow my car for a few hours that evening. I left the keys with the coworker and went to bed.\""), .direct("Why were you at the gas station at 4:10?", "\"I got up early to fill the tank before work. I didn't notice anything unusual, and I used my own card.\""), .direct("How did you come to be at that gas station at 4:10 in the morning?", "\"I work early and often fill up before a shift. I stopped at the pump and paid for my own gas, and I never touched a stolen card.\""), .cross("The stolen card was used at that gas station, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, but I did not use it. I bought gas with my own money.\""), .cross("The gas station camera shows you at the pump, doesn't it?", "\"It does. I was buying gas. I know the timing looks bad, but I did not take that card.\""), .cross("You say you found the card. Where?", "\"I found it on the ground at the gas station. I should have handed it in.\""), .cross("The stolen card was used at the same station you were at. How do you explain that?", "\"I don't know. I didn't use it and I didn't see anyone else using it. It's a station a lot of people use.\""), .cross("You say a coworker borrowed the car. Why would the coworker deny it?", "\"I don't know why. I told you what I remember, and I can't account for what the coworker says.\"")],
        openings: ("At 3 a.m., a homeowner woke to a barking dog and found the kitchen door open and a purse gone. A neighbor's camera recorded a plate belonging to {D}, and the stolen card was used at a gas station an hour later.", "Jurors will hear that {D} lent the car to a coworker and never entered the house. The card came into {D}'s hands by chance."),
        closings: ("A car leaving at 3:05, a plate that belongs to {D}, and a stolen card used at 4:10 at a pump where {D} was filmed. The timeline is not a coincidence.", "A homeowner who did not see the driver, a car that was lent, and a card that was found. The State has put a car at a house, not {D}."),
        timeline: [(0, "3 a.m.: the kitchen door opens."), (0, "3:05 a.m.: a car leaves the street."), (0, "4:10 a.m.: the stolen card is used.")],
        identified: "A plate and a card charge.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I lock every door twice.")

    static let tireIronAssault = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.tireIronAssault",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Man Struck With Tire Iron During Parking Dispute", "Motorist Needs Surgery for Fractured Forearm"],
        law: "awdwisi",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Assaulted {V} with a deadly weapon, a tire iron, inflicting serious injury, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 23...58,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A parking space dispute at a shopping center on {DATE} ended with {V} struck on the forearm with a tire iron. {V} needed surgery. A witness saw {D} take a tire iron from a trunk. {DL} says {V} lunged and {D.he} swung in fear.",
        state: [E(.statement, 3, "Witness", "{D} took a tire iron from a trunk and swung."), E(.forensic, 3, "Medical Records", "A fractured forearm requiring surgery.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lunged", "{DL} says {V} lunged first.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What did the witness tell you?", "\"The witness said {D} took a tire iron from a trunk and swung it at {V} during a parking dispute.\""), .direct("What was {V}'s injury?", "\"A fractured forearm that needed surgery. The medical records document it.\""), .direct("What was the dispute about?", "\"A parking space at a shopping center. It escalated from words to a physical attack.\""), .direct("What did you find when you arrived at the shopping center?", "\"{V} was sitting on the curb holding an arm that was visibly bent. A tire iron lay on the pavement near a gray sedan with its trunk open.\""), .direct("What did the witness tell you about the trunk?", "\"The witness said {D} walked to the car, opened the trunk, took out the tire iron, and came back toward {V}. The witness saw the swing and heard a crack.\""), .direct("What did the medical records show?", "\"A fractured forearm that needed surgery, with a plate placed to hold the bone. The doctors told me recovery would take months.\""), .cross("{D} says {V} lunged first, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {D} says. The witness did not see a lunge.\""), .cross("A tire iron is a tool, isn't it?", "\"It is a tool, but it was used here as a weapon.\""), .cross("Did {V} move toward {D} before the swing?", "\"I was told there may have been movement. I cannot confirm what it was.\""), .cross("Did you see the swing yourself?", "\"No. I arrived after the fact, and I only know what the witness and the parties told me.\""), .cross("Did you find any injury on {D}?", "\"A scrape on one hand and a bruise on a wrist. {D} said {V} grabbed {D.him} during the argument.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's passenger",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What did you see?", "\"I saw {V} step toward {D} during the argument. It was aggressive, and it got {D}'s attention.\""), .direct("How close did {V} come?", "\"A few feet. {V} was close enough that I thought there might be a fight.\""), .direct("What did {D} do?", "\"{D} went to the trunk and grabbed the tire iron. Then it all happened quickly.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"I was a passenger in {D}'s car that day. We'd been shopping together and we're friends.\""), .direct("What did you see right before the swing?", "\"{V} was yelling and walked up very close to {D}. {V} had a fist raised when I looked over.\""), .direct("What did {D} do afterward?", "\"{D} dropped the tire iron and looked shocked. {D} said {D.he} was sorry and told me to call 911.\""), .cross("How far away was {V}?", "\"A few feet. I would say within arm's reach, but not touching.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} swing at anyone?", "\"No. I did not see {V} swing. I saw {V} step forward.\""), .cross("Could anything have blocked your view?", "\"There was a post in the way, so I might have missed something.\""), .cross("How far were you from {D} when it happened?", "\"About twenty feet, across the lot. A concrete post was between us, so I couldn't see everything.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} touch {D}?", "\"No. I saw {V} move toward {D} but I can't say that a hand reached {D}.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} struck a driver with a tire iron.", "A swing in fear."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for the damage I did.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} walked past a closer door to reach the trunk.", "The passenger's view was blocked by a post."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you swing the tire iron?", "\"Yes, I did. {V} came at me, and I was afraid. I grabbed it and swung.\""), .direct("Why did you go to the trunk?", "\"I wanted something to protect myself. It was the only thing I had.\""), .direct("Did you mean to break {V}'s arm?", "\"No. I did not mean to hurt {V.him} like that. I just wanted {V.him} to stop.\""), .direct("Tell the jury what started the argument.", "\"We both wanted the same parking space. I'd pulled in first and {V} came up behind me and said I'd cut {V.him} off.\""), .direct("What did you do when {V} came toward you?", "\"I stepped back, and {V} kept coming and raised a hand. I turned toward my trunk and took out the tire iron because I thought I was in danger.\""), .direct("What happened when you swung?", "\"I swung at {V}'s arm to stop {V.him}. I didn't aim for {V.his} head, and I never meant to break anything.\""), .cross("You walked past a closer door to reach the trunk, didn't you?", "\"The trunk was where the iron was. I did not think about doors.\""), .cross("A fractured forearm needing surgery. Isn't that serious?", "\"Very serious, and I apologize. I never wanted that.\""), .cross("You could have driven away instead, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have. I was angry and scared.\""), .cross("You walked to your trunk. Couldn't you have gotten into your car and locked the door?", "\"I thought about it, but {V} was too close. It seemed like I had only seconds.\""), .cross("Why a tire iron instead of walking away?", "\"It was the only thing I had. I wasn't thinking clearly, and I'm very sorry for what happened.\"")],
        openings: ("A parking space dispute at a shopping center ended with {V} struck on the forearm with a tire iron and needing surgery. A witness saw {D} take it from a trunk and swing.", "{D} swung only after {V} lunged. The defense will show a frightened reaction in a parking lot, not a planned attack, and a person who never wanted anyone hurt."),
        closings: ("{D} walked to a trunk, took out a tire iron, and swung it at {V}'s arm. A fractured forearm and a surgery are the result.", "{V} lunged and {D} swung in fear. The law gives every person the right to protect against attack, and that is what happened."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 p.m.: the parking dispute."), (0, "1:05 p.m.: {DL} goes to the trunk."), (0, "1:06 p.m.: the swing."), (0, "1:25 p.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "A witness.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant was armed with a deadly weapon at the time of the crime"],
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["selfDefense"],
        genders: ["V": .male])

    static let photoExtortion = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.photoExtortion",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Man Demands $3,000 or Photos Go to Boss and Family", "Texts Show Escalating Demands"],
        law: "extortion",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Threatened {V} with the release of private photographs to obtain $3,000, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...55,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} received texts from an unknown number on {DATE} demanding $3,000 or private photos would go to {V}'s employer and family. The number traced to a prepaid phone bought by {D}, who had once dated {V}. {DL} says {D.he} lost the phone and never sent anything.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Texts", "'$3,000 by Friday or everyone sees them.'"), E(.document, 3, "Prepaid Receipt", "{D} bought the phone and paid cash.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lost Phone", "{DL} says {D.he} lost the phone.")],
        role: "Victim",
        exam: [.direct("What did the texts say?", "\"They said '$3,000 by Friday or everyone sees them.' It came from a number I did not know.\""), .direct("Who had the photos?", "\"Only {D}. The photos were private, and I had shared them with no one else.\""), .direct("How did you learn who owned the phone?", "\"Deputies traced the number to a prepaid phone. The receipt shows {D} bought it with cash.\""), .direct("What did the first text say, and what did you think?", "\"'$3,000 by Friday or everyone sees them.' I didn't recognize the number and I didn't know what photos it meant until a second message included one.\""), .direct("What did the second message include?", "\"A photo that had been private, which I'd shared only with {D} when we were together. It was attached to a reminder of the deadline.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I blocked the number, called the sheriff's office, and screenshotted everything. A deputy told me the number was a prepaid phone.\""), .cross("Someone else could have had those photos, couldn't they?", "\"Not these. They were only ever in one place, and {D} had them.\""), .cross("The number was unknown to you, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not know it. It was traced to a prepaid phone bought by {D}.\""), .cross("You and {D} dated once, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It ended, and we were not on good terms.\""), .cross("Did you ever see {D} with the phone?", "\"No. I only know what the deputy told me, that {D} bought it with cash at a store.\""), .cross("Could someone else have gotten the photos, such as through a shared cloud account?", "\"I don't think so. I deleted them from my own phone and cloud a long time ago, and only {D} would have had them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} tried to extort a former partner.", "A lost phone."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I was desperate.\"",
        truths: ("The photos were sent from a cloud account that only {DL} used.", "The prepaid phone's receipt bore a signature that was not {DL}'s."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you send those texts?", "\"No. I did not send anything. I never threatened {V.him} and never planned to.\""), .direct("What happened to the prepaid phone?", "\"I lost it. I looked everywhere and never found it, and I did not know who had it.\""), .direct("Do you know how the photos got out?", "\"I do not. My cloud account may have been hacked, and I did not know about it.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your relationship with {V}.", "\"We dated for about a year and broke up on bad terms. We haven't spoken much since, and I have no hard feelings.\""), .direct("Tell the jury about the phone.", "\"I bought a prepaid phone as a backup for work. I lost it a week or so later and couldn't find it.\""), .direct("Do you still have the photos?", "\"I did on an old cloud account, and I don't use it anymore. Someone could have gotten into it, since I never changed the password.\""), .cross("The photos came from a cloud account only you used, didn't they?", "\"I thought only I used it. Someone must have gotten in.\""), .cross("You owed {V} money, didn't you?", "\"Yes, a debt. It was small, and I was working on it.\""), .cross("The prepaid receipt shows you bought the phone in cash. Why?", "\"I like to pay in cash. I bought it for a few weeks, and then I lost it.\""), .cross("The receipt shows you bought the phone with cash. Why pay cash?", "\"I always do for small purchases. It's not something I do to hide things.\""), .cross("The photos came from a cloud account you used. Doesn't that point to you?", "\"It points to my account, but anyone who got into it could have sent them. I never sent a message to {V}.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} received texts from an unknown number demanding $3,000 or private photos would go to {V}'s employer and family. The number traced to a prepaid phone bought by {D}, who once dated {V}.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {D} lost that phone and never sent a thing. Someone else had access, and nothing proves {D} typed those words."),
        closings: ("Photos that only {D} had, a prepaid phone bought by {D}, and a demand for $3,000. That is extortion by the person who held the photos.", "A lost phone, a cloud account that may have been hacked, and no proof of who typed those words. Suspicion is not enough, and the State has not done more."),
        timeline: [(-3, "{DL} buys the prepaid phone."), (0, "The first demand."), (2, "The deadline passes."), (3, "{V} reports it.")],
        identified: "A prepaid receipt and cloud records.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I was terrified for my job.",
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let inspectorBribe = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.inspectorBribe",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Contractor Hands Building Inspector Envelope With $1,500", "Inspector Wore Recorder at Final Walk-Through"],
        law: "bribery",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Offered a thing of value to {V}, a public official, to influence an official act, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 30...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A building inspector, {V}, was handed an envelope containing $1,500 at a final walk-through on {DATE} by {D}, a contractor, and told to 'overlook the wiring.' {V} wore a recorder at the request of investigators after earlier hints. {DL} says it was a thank-you gift. The recording captures {D} saying 'overlook the wiring and there's more.' The wiring had failed inspection before, and {D} had asked {V} for a pass the day before the walk-through.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Recording", "{D}: 'Overlook the wiring and there's more.'"), E(.physical, 3, "Envelope", "An envelope with $1,500.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Thank-You", "{DL} says it was a thank-you gift.")],
        role: "Building inspector",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I'm a building inspector for the county. I review plans, inspect work, and sign off on projects that meet the code.\""), .direct("What was {D}'s project?", "\"A building where {D} was the contractor. The wiring had failed inspection twice, about two weeks before the final walk-through.\""), .direct("What happened the day before the walk-through?", "\"{D} called and asked me for a pass on the wiring. I said I'd have to see it, and the issues had to be fixed.\""), .direct("Why did you wear a recorder?", "\"Earlier hints from {D} made me uneasy, so I told investigators and they asked me to record the final walk-through.\""), .direct("What happened at the walk-through on {DATE}?", "\"{D} handed me an envelope with $1,500 in it and said, Overlook the wiring and there's more.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I took the envelope, left, and gave everything to the investigators. I never intended to keep it.\""), .cross("Isn't it true {D} said it was a thank-you?", "\"{D} called it that afterward. At the time, {D} said to overlook the wiring, so I understood it differently.\""), .cross("Do contractors give holiday gifts?", "\"Sometimes small ones. Anything of value is against county rules, and I decline them.\""), .cross("Did you open the envelope in front of {D}?", "\"I looked inside, and I saw the cash. I told {D} nothing and left.\""), .cross("Did you ask {D} to hand you anything?", "\"No. I didn't hint or request anything. The recording speaks for itself.\""), .cross("How many times did the wiring fail?", "\"Twice, and there were real problems. That's why I knew a pass was out of the question.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} bribed an inspector.", "A thank-you."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I knew better.\"",
        truths: ("The wiring had failed inspection twice.", "The envelope held a holiday gift card from a list the contractor gave every inspector."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you give {V} an envelope?", "\"It was a thank-you for the work on the project. I give small gifts at the end of a job as a courtesy.\""), .direct("What was in the envelope?", "\"A gift, as I recall. I didn't count it, and I wasn't thinking about the contents.\""), .direct("What did you mean by, Overlook the wiring?", "\"I was joking in a clumsy way about the small stuff. I was nervous, and I said it badly.\""), .direct("Why did you ask for a pass the day before?", "\"Because I'd been told the work was nearly finished, and I wanted the job closed. I didn't expect to cut corners.\""), .direct("Did you intend to bribe {V}?", "\"No. I've never offered anything like that. I'm a contractor trying to finish a project.\""), .direct("What happened when you learned about the recording?", "\"I was shocked. I told the investigators the envelope was a gift and that I'd said it as a joke.\""), .cross("The recording says, Overlook the wiring and there's more, doesn't it?", "\"It does. I know how it sounds, and I regret how I said it.\""), .cross("The wiring had failed inspection twice?", "\"Yes. We were fixing it, and I thought it was close.\""), .cross("You asked for a pass the day before?", "\"I asked if it could be done. I didn't think it was improper to ask.\""), .cross("You handed over $1,500?", "\"The investigators say there was $1,500. I can't swear to the amount, and I didn't intend it as payment.\""), .cross("You give such gifts to every inspector?", "\"I give a holiday gift to the people I work with. It's a list I keep, and I was following it.\"")],
        openings: ("At a final walk-through, {D} handed building inspector {V} an envelope with $1,500 and said, Overlook the wiring and there's more. The wiring had failed inspection twice, {D} had asked for a pass the day before, and a recorder captured every word.", "{D} meant the envelope as a holiday thank-you, as {D} does for every inspector, and the words were a clumsy joke. The defense says a gift on a contractor's list is not a bribe."),
        closings: ("A recording, an envelope of $1,500, and two failed inspections. {D} asked for a pass, handed over cash, and promised more, which is a bribe.", "A holiday list, a gift card in an envelope, and a nervous joke. The State must prove {D} intended to corrupt an official, and the words alone do not prove it."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The first failed inspection."), (-1, "{DL} asks for a pass."), (0, "The walk-through and envelope.")],
        identified: "A recording.",
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let investmentClub = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.investmentClub",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Investment Club Founder Accused of Using Members' Money for Home", "Bank Records Show Purchases, Not Trades"],
        law: "securitiesFraud",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Obtained $62,000 from {V}, an investor, by false statements about securities, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 35...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} ran an investment club that collected $62,000 from {V} and others, promising monthly returns from trading. Records showed no trades; the money paid for a home addition and a boat. {DL} says trades lost money and records were incomplete.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Records", "No brokerage activity; payments for a home addition and boat."), E(.document, 2, "Club Statements", "Monthly returns reported with no trades.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Losses", "{DL} says trades lost money.")],
        role: "Investor",
        exam: [.direct("How did you become involved with {D}'s investment club?", "\"A friend told me about it. {D} promised monthly returns from trading, and I invested my savings.\""), .direct("How much did you invest?", "\"I put in thousands of dollars, and the club collected $62,000 from me and other members in total.\""), .direct("What did {D} send you each month?", "\"A statement showing returns. They looked professional and listed gains every month.\""), .direct("What happened when you asked to withdraw?", "\"{D} stalled. I asked again after a week, and the answers became vague, so I went to the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What did investigators find?", "\"Bank records showed no brokerage activity. The money paid for a home addition and a boat.\""), .direct("What did that do to you?", "\"I lost the money I'd saved for retirement. I trusted {D}, and I'm embarrassed to say I never asked for proof.\""), .cross("Isn't it true you never saw a brokerage statement?", "\"Right. I only saw the monthly sheets from {D}. I never asked for outside proof.\""), .cross("Did you read the club agreement?", "\"I skimmed it. It said trading involves risk, and I understood that, but I assumed trading was happening.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever say the club was making money?", "\"Every month. The statements showed gains, and that's what kept me in.\""), .cross("Did other members have the same experience?", "\"Yes, several. We compared notes and everyone had the same kind of statement.\""), .cross("Were any funds returned?", "\"No. None of us got our money back.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Forensic accountant",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role in this case?", "\"I'm a forensic accountant. I reviewed {D}'s records, the bank statements, and the club's reports.\""), .direct("What did you review?", "\"Bank records, club statements, and a set of brokerage documents that {D} provided. The records were incomplete.\""), .direct("What did the bank records show?", "\"Deposits from members, payments for a home addition and a boat, and transfers to a brokerage firm.\""), .direct("What was missing?", "\"Some trading records and several months of account statements. I couldn't fully reconstruct the trading.\""), .direct("Could trading losses explain some of the shortfall?", "\"They could explain part of it, but I couldn't say how much without the missing records.\""), .direct("What do you conclude?", "\"That the records are too incomplete to say exactly where each dollar went. A complete audit would take more documents.\""), .cross("You found payments to a home addition and boat, didn't you?", "\"Yes. Those are clear in the bank records, and they are not trading expenses.\""), .cross("The monthly statements to members were not real statements?", "\"They were summary sheets on a template. I wouldn't call them accurate reports of any account.\""), .cross("You were paid by the defense?", "\"Yes, I'm compensated for my time. I'm giving my professional opinion, not an advocate's argument.\""), .cross("Did the bank records show gains?", "\"No. They show no gains that would support monthly returns.\""), .cross("You can't say that most of the money went to trading?", "\"No. I can only say trading took some, and personal spending took some.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} spent members' money on a house and boat.", "Trading losses."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I lost control.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} created fake statements on a template.", "A real brokerage statement showed {DL} lost $48,000 of the club's money in trades."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was the club?", "\"A group of friends and neighbors who pooled money for trading. I made the trades and sent reports.\""), .direct("Did you trade with the money?", "\"Yes. I made trades in a brokerage account, and many lost money. I ought to have watched those trades much more closely.\""), .direct("Why did the statements show gains?", "\"I was embarrassed by the losses. I made summary sheets on a template and showed returns I'd hoped to get.\""), .direct("What about the home addition and boat?", "\"Some of the money went to my own expenses. I told myself I'd put it back once the trades turned around.\""), .direct("How much did you lose in trading?", "\"A lot, close to $48,000 over time. I didn't tell the members, and I should have.\""), .direct("What would you tell the members?", "\"I am truly sorry. I meant to make it right, and I didn't have the courage to tell them it was going wrong.\""), .cross("The bank records show no brokerage activity, don't they?", "\"Some of the activity was in a separate account. The records may not show all of it.\""), .cross("You made up the statements?", "\"I made summary sheets from a template. I didn't call them fake at the time, but they weren't accurate.\""), .cross("You spent members' money on a boat?", "\"Part of it, yes. I know it was wrong.\""), .cross("Members asked to withdraw and you stalled?", "\"Yes. I didn't have the money, and I panicked.\""), .cross("You never told anyone about the losses?", "\"No, not until it all came apart. I was hoping to recover.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} ran an investment club that collected $62,000 from {V} and others, promising monthly returns from trading. Bank records show no trades for most of it, and the money paid for a home addition and a boat.", "{D} did trade and lost money, and the paperwork was messy rather than a scheme. The defense says the State must prove {D} never meant to trade, and the records are too incomplete."),
        closings: ("Sixty-two thousand dollars, monthly statements with no trades behind them, and a home addition and a boat. {V} and others trusted {D} with their savings.", "A forensic accountant could not say where each dollar went, and trading did lose money. Poor bookkeeping and bad investing are not the same as a scheme to defraud."),
        timeline: [(-300, "The club forms."), (-180, "The first false statement."), (0, "{V} asks to withdraw."), (7, "The accountant reviews the records.")],
        identified: "Bank records and statements.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "Our retirement was gone.")

    static let payrollClerkTheft = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.payrollClerkTheft",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Payroll Clerk Redirected Pay Into Own Account for Two Years", "Audit Shows Dozens of Rerouted Deposits"],
        law: "embezzlement100k",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Embezzled over $100,000 entrusted to {D} by {V}, an employer, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 30...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "An audit on {DATE} found $128,000 in payroll deposits rerouted to an account opened by {D}, the payroll clerk, over two years, using terminated employees' names. {DL} says the accounts were set up by a prior clerk and {D.he} followed the system. The edits were made under {D}'s login, and the first rerouted deposit came about ten days after {D} became the payroll clerk two years earlier.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Audit", "$128,000 rerouted to {D}'s account."), E(.digital, 3, "System Logs", "Edits made under {D}'s login.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Prior Clerk", "{DL} says a prior clerk set up the accounts.")],
        role: "Company owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did the audit find?", "\"$128,000 in payroll deposits were rerouted to an account opened by {D}, the payroll clerk, over two years.\""), .direct("How were the deposits sent?", "\"They used the names of terminated employees. The edits were made under {D}'s login.\""), .direct("When did it start?", "\"The first rerouted deposit came about ten days after {D} became the payroll clerk.\""), .direct("How was the fraud discovered?", "\"An outside auditor compared payroll totals with the bank statements and found deposits to accounts for employees we'd let go. The money was all going to one account.\""), .direct("How large was the diversion, and over what period?", "\"$128,000 over twenty-four months, in amounts of a few hundred to a couple thousand dollars each pay period.\""), .direct("What did the system logs show?", "\"Edits to the direct-deposit records made under {D}'s login, usually late in the day. The first edit was ten days after {D} began the job.\""), .cross("A prior clerk could have set up those accounts, couldn't a prior clerk?", "\"The prior clerk left before. I cannot say who set up the accounts.\""), .cross("The system allowed such edits, didn't it?", "\"Yes. The system was not designed to stop it, and I know that is on us.\""), .cross("Did others have access to the payroll system?", "\"Some had access, yes. The logs show {D}'s login for these edits.\""), .cross("Who else had access to payroll?", "\"A few of us, including me and an outside accountant. The system allowed edits from several logins, which I now realize was a problem.\""), .cross("Did you look at the account the money went to?", "\"It was opened under {D}'s name. I can't say who typed the application, only that the account holder is {D}.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Prior payroll clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you create those accounts?", "\"No. I did not create those accounts. I never set up an account for a terminated employee.\""), .direct("When did you leave the company?", "\"In 2019. I left before {D} started, so I could not have done any of it.\""), .direct("How did the payroll system work then?", "\"It was simple. We had one login each, and the system was not locked down.\""), .direct("What was your job at the company before {D}?", "\"I was the payroll clerk for three years. I left when I got another job, before {D} was hired.\""), .direct("How was the payroll system set up when you worked there?", "\"One login each, but the system didn't track who edited which record. Anyone with a password could change deposit information.\""), .direct("Did you set up any account for someone who did not work there?", "\"No. I never created an account for an employee who wasn't on the payroll.\""), .cross("Why do you think {D} did it?", "\"I do not know. I can only say it was not me.\""), .cross("Did anyone else have access when you were there?", "\"Yes. The owner's relatives had access too, I believe.\""), .cross("Do you have proof you did not create the accounts?", "\"The dates show I left in 2019. That is what I can offer.\""), .cross("Were there any suspicious accounts when you left?", "\"None that I knew of. I didn't audit the records, so I can't say if anything was missing.\""), .cross("Who trained {D} on the system?", "\"I did, for about a week before I left. I showed {D} how to add and remove employees, and I gave {D} my notes.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} diverted payroll.", "A system handed down."),
        allocution: "\"I took it. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("Rerouted deposits began the week {DL} took over.", "Payroll access was shared with the owner's brother, who set up the account."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you divert the payroll deposits?", "\"No. I did not divert anything. I followed the system I was given.\""), .direct("Who set up the accounts?", "\"They were set up by the prior clerk. I assumed they were legitimate when I started.\""), .direct("Why were the edits under your login?", "\"The login was shared at times. Other people had access, and I did not guard it as In hindsight, yes.\""), .direct("What can you tell us about your job as payroll clerk?", "\"I processed payroll every two weeks, set up new hires, and removed people who left. The company relied on me and one other clerk, who'd quit before I started.\""), .direct("Describe the accounts you inherited in your own words.", "\"When I started, there were a few accounts set up for employees I didn't recognize. I assumed they were contractors the prior clerk had added.\""), .direct("Why was your login used for the edits?", "\"The login was shared between a few of us when someone was out. I didn't think it was a problem, and I'd leave it logged in sometimes.\""), .cross("The first deposit came ten days after you started, didn't it?", "\"I do not know about that. I did not notice a thing like that.\""), .cross("$128,000 went to an account opened by you. How is that not you?", "\"I did not open it. The records say I did, but I never remember doing it.\""), .cross("What was that money used for?", "\"I do not know. I did not take it.\""), .cross("The first diverted deposit was ten days after you started. Is that a coincidence?", "\"I don't know. I wasn't tracking that detail, and I didn't make that edit.\""), .cross("Money went to an account opened in your name. How could anyone else have opened it?", "\"I didn't open that account. Someone used my information, or I was given forms that I signed without reading.\"")],
        openings: ("An audit found $128,000 in payroll deposits rerouted over two years to an account opened by {D}, the payroll clerk, using terminated employees' names, with edits made under {D}'s login.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that the accounts predate {D} and that the payroll login was shared. The system allowed anyone with access to do this."),
        closings: ("Two years, $128,000, a login that belongs to {D}, and an account opened by {D}. The first rerouted deposit came ten days after {D} took the job.", "A shared login and a system that anyone could edit. The State has shown that money moved, not who moved it, and doubt remains about who did."),
        timeline: [(-730, "{DL} becomes payroll clerk."), (-720, "The first rerouted deposit."), (0, "The audit begins."), (10, "The owner reads the report.")],
        identified: "An audit and system logs.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let contractKillingPlot = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.contractKillingPlot",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Husband Offered Hitman $5,000 to Kill Wife, Undercover Says", "Recorded Meeting at a Diner Leads to Arrest"],
        law: "attemptedMurder1",
        threshold: 9,
        spec: "Took overt steps to have {V} killed with malice, premeditation, and deliberation by paying another to do it, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 30...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "An informant told deputies that {D} wanted to hire someone to kill {V}, {D.his} spouse, for $5,000. An undercover deputy met {D} at a diner on {DATE}, and {D} handed over $2,500 and a photo of {V}. {DL} says {D.he} was venting and never meant it.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Recording", "{D}: 'Make it look like a robbery.'"), E(.physical, 3, "Cash and Photo", "$2,500 and a photo of {V}.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Venting", "{DL} says {D.he} was venting.")],
        role: "Undercover deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What was your role in this operation?", "\"I'm an undercover deputy. An informant told us {D} wanted someone hired to kill {D}'s spouse for $5,000.\""), .direct("What happened at the diner on {DATE}?", "\"I met {D} in a booth. We talked about the job, and {D} handed me $2,500 and a photo of {V}.\""), .direct("What did {D} say?", "\"{D} said, Make it look like a robbery. It was recorded on my wire, and I've reviewed it for accuracy.\""), .direct("How did the conversation begin?", "\"I introduced myself as the person the informant mentioned and asked what {D} wanted done.\""), .direct("Did {D} discuss the price?", "\"Yes. We agreed on $5,000, and {D} gave me half up front. {D} said the rest would come after.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I signaled the arrest team and {D} was taken into custody in the parking lot, with the photo and the rest of the plan.\""), .cross("Isn't it true you raised the plan and the $2,500 first?", "\"I steered the conversation, as undercover work requires. {D} then agreed and brought the money.\""), .cross("Did {D} say, I don't know, at any point?", "\"Yes, more than once. {D} hesitated several times before saying, Make it look like a robbery.\""), .cross("Did {D} initiate contact with you?", "\"The informant set up the meeting. I didn't have a prior relationship with {D}.\""), .cross("Was {D} intoxicated or upset?", "\"{D} seemed upset and nervous. I don't recall any signs of alcohol.\""), .cross("Did {D} ask for a particular date?", "\"No. {D} didn't specify a date or place for the killing.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's friend",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"{D} is a close friend. We've known each other for years, and I've seen {D} through a lot.\""), .direct("What was {D} going through?", "\"A hard marriage. {D} was hurt and angry and talked to me a lot about it.\""), .direct("Did {D} ever say anything about harming {V}?", "\"Never seriously. {D} sometimes said things like, I could just disappear, but never about hurting anyone.\""), .direct("What kind of person is {D}?", "\"Gentle. {D} has never raised a hand to anyone, and I've never seen {D} violent.\""), .direct("How did {D} react to the arrest?", "\"Devastated. {D} told me it was a stupid mistake and that {D.he} never meant it.\""), .direct("Did {D} talk about money or insurance?", "\"Not that I recall. {D} never mentioned any plan involving money.\""), .cross("You didn't know about the meeting with the deputy, did you?", "\"No. I had no idea {D} was meeting anyone like that.\""), .cross("{D} told you about wanting someone to disappear?", "\"Venting, like many people do. I didn't take it as a plan.\""), .cross("You can't say what {D} meant at the diner?", "\"No. I wasn't there. I only know {D}'s character.\""), .cross("{D} is your friend, isn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. I'm trying to tell the truth about what I know.\""), .cross("You never saw {D} with a large amount of cash?", "\"No, not until I heard about the arrest.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} paid for a killing.", "A man venting."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I don't know what I was thinking.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had changed a life insurance beneficiary the week before.", "The undercover deputy raised the plan and the $2,500 first, and {DL} said 'I don't know' three times."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you meet the undercover deputy?", "\"An acquaintance said someone could help with my marriage troubles. I thought I'd listen, and I was venting.\""), .direct("What were you thinking?", "\"I was angry and hurt, and I said things I didn't mean. I never planned to follow through on any of it.\""), .direct("Why did you bring $2,500 and a photo?", "\"Because the deputy asked for them, and I felt pressured. I thought I could hand them over and then back out.\""), .direct("What did you mean by, Make it look like a robbery?", "\"I was repeating what the deputy had suggested. It was a dark thing to say, and it came out of anger.\""), .direct("Did you intend to harm {V}?", "\"No. I love {V}, and we've been through a hard time. I never meant for anyone to be hurt.\""), .direct("What would you say to {V}?", "\"I'm sorry for what I said. I was in a bad place, and I'm getting help.\""), .cross("You handed over $2,500, didn't you?", "\"I did. It was my money, and I'm ashamed that I brought it.\""), .cross("You changed the beneficiary on a life insurance policy the week before?", "\"I did. It was something I'd been meaning to do, and the timing was bad.\""), .cross("You gave the deputy a photo of your spouse?", "\"Yes. I had it in my wallet, and I gave it over without thinking.\""), .cross("You said it should look like a robbery?", "\"Those are my words on the recording. I can't take them back.\""), .cross("You never called the whole thing off?", "\"I didn't have the chance. I was arrested before I could.\"")],
        openings: ("An informant told deputies that {D} wanted to hire someone to kill {V}, {D.his} spouse, for $5,000. At a diner on {DATE}, {D} handed an undercover deputy $2,500 and a photo of {V} and said, Make it look like a robbery.", "{D} was venting about a painful marriage, hesitated repeatedly, and was led along by an undercover deputy who raised the plan and the money first. The defense says words said in anger and a deputy's push are not a real contract."),
        closings: ("The recording, the $2,500, and the photo of {V}. A person who brings cash and a picture to a meeting has gone beyond talk, and a beneficiary change the week before explains the motive.", "The deputy raised the plan and the money, and {D} said, I don't know, three times. The State must prove a genuine intent, and a hesitant person led by an undercover agent leaves doubt."),
        timeline: [(-14, "{DL} changes the insurance beneficiary."), (-7, "An informant calls deputies."), (0, "The diner meeting."), (0, "{DL} is arrested.")],
        identified: "An undercover recording.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I live with someone who wanted me dead.",
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let boatCrashFatal = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.boatCrashFatal",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Passenger Dies After Boat Hits Dock at Night", "Skipper Had Been Drinking All Afternoon, Marine Officer Says"],
        law: "invManslaughter",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Unlawfully killed {V} without malice by a culpably negligent act, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 25...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A boat driven by {D} struck a dock at 9:30 p.m. on {DATE} at about 35 mph, killing {V}, a passenger. A marine officer found {D} with a 0.12. No navigation lights were on. {DL} says a wake threw the boat and the lights burned out.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Blood Test", "0.12 about an hour after."), E(.physical, 3, "Boat Lights", "The navigation light switch was off.", .search), E(.document, 2, "Speed Estimate", "About 35 mph at impact.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Wake", "{DL} says a wake threw the boat.")],
        role: "Marine patrol officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you respond to on {DATE}?", "\"A boat crash into a dock at about 9:30 p.m. {V}, a passenger, was killed, and the boat was badly damaged.\""), .direct("What did you find at the scene?", "\"The boat had hit a dock at speed. There were no navigation lights on, and the light switch was in the off position.\""), .direct("What was {D}'s condition?", "\"{D} smelled of alcohol and was shaken. A blood test about an hour later showed 0.12.\""), .direct("How fast was the boat going?", "\"About 35 mph at impact, based on damage and witness accounts. That's fast for a dark night near shore.\""), .direct("What did the afternoon look like?", "\"The group went out around 2 p.m. and spent the day on the lake. They started home around 9:20 p.m.\""), .direct("What did you find in the boat?", "\"A cooler under the seat with empty cans. I couldn't tell how many each person had.\""), .cross("Isn't it true a large wake can throw a boat?", "\"It can. I've seen it happen, and a big wake can change a boat's course.\""), .cross("Did you see a wake that night?", "\"No. I arrived after the crash. {D} said a wake threw the boat, and I can't confirm it.\""), .cross("Were the lights working?", "\"The switch was off. I don't know if the bulbs or the fuse were good.\""), .cross("Was {D} cooperative?", "\"Yes. {D} was distraught and gave a full statement. {D} tried to help {V} and called for help.\""), .cross("Did the 0.12 reading account for the delay?", "\"The test was an hour after, so {D}'s level at 9:30 could have been higher. I can't say.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Boat mechanic",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do for a living?", "\"I'm a boat mechanic. I repair and service boats, including their electrical systems and navigation lights.\""), .direct("Do you know {D}'s boat?", "\"Yes. I've worked on it a few times, including its wiring.\""), .direct("How do the navigation lights work on that model?", "\"They're on a fused circuit with a switch at the helm. The fuse is a common failure point.\""), .direct("Have you seen those fuses blow?", "\"Often. I've replaced them on that model many times, usually after a wet or rough day.\""), .direct("When did you last see the boat before the crash?", "\"A few days earlier, for general service. {D} was careful and asked good questions.\""), .direct("What kind of boater is {D}?", "\"Safe, I always thought. {D} follows the rules and asks for advice.\""), .cross("You didn't examine the boat after the crash, did you?", "\"No. It was towed away and I wasn't involved.\""), .cross("You can't say the lights were off because of a blown fuse?", "\"I can't say for that night. I only know that the fuse often fails.\""), .cross("The switch was found off?", "\"So I heard. That's something the boater controls.\""), .cross("You can't say anything about {D}'s drinking?", "\"No. I wasn't there, and I only know {D} from the shop.\""), .cross("You're a friend of {D}'s?", "\"I'm a business acquaintance. I'm giving you my professional opinion.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove a boat drunk without lights and killed a passenger.", "A wake and a dead bulb."),
